.TH GEN 1 "November 2026" "ix"
.SH NAME
gen \- ask a generator or fetch and install ports
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gen ask
.RI [ effort ]
.br
.B gen list
.br
.B gen fetch
.RI [ organization/repository ]
.br
.B gen install
.I organization/repository
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ask
passes standard input to the executable named by
.B GEN_AGENT
and relays its standard output. The executable receives
.B GEN_EFFORT
in its environment. gen can select a configured HTTP endpoint or a local
Codex CLI.
.PP
Ports are Git repositories. Fetch puts a checkout in
.BR $HOME/src .
Install runs the port's Makefile. The default prefix is
.B /
for root and
.B $HOME
otherwise.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B GEN_PORTS
names the ports Makefile.
.B GIT_ROOT
selects its Git mirror.
.B GEN_URL
and
.B GEN_MODEL
configure gen-http.
.B GEN_KEY
is its optional bearer token.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR yhwh (1),
.BR lord (1),
.BR ix (1)
